 class=3D"elementToProof">
<b>Director Sumption</b>,</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
I am writing this letter publicly because private channels have been met wi=
th silence, and the issues at stake extend far beyond my individual experie=
nce. I want to begin by acknowledging what you have built during your tenur=
e at
<b>Oregon Parks &amp; Recreation Department</b>, an institution I had remar=
kable respect for, that I wanted to be part of, that I wanted to support an=
d grow with.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 2rem; margin=
: 3rem 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
<b>Recognition Where It's Due</b></div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
Your career speaks to genuine dedication to public service. As the first wo=
man to lead OPRD, you have overseen millions in infrastructure investments,=
 championed diversity and accessibility initiatives, and built a national r=
eputation for leadership through
 your role as President of the National Association of State Park Directors=
. Your recent appointment to the National Parks Service Advisory Board refl=
ects the respect you have earned in the field.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
The statements you have made publicly about breaking down barriers and ensu=
ring that Oregon's parks welcome everyone resonate with the values that bro=
ught me to volunteer at Honeyman in the first place. I believed then, as I =
believe now, that parks should be
 spaces where all people can serve and find belonging.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 2rem; margin=
: 3rem 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
<b>Silence Is Not Neutral</b></div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
Earlier this year, I served as an unpaid volunteer at Honeyman State Park. =
What I experienced there was not a miscommunication or personality conflict=
. It was systematic institutional misconduct executed against someone servi=
ng without compensation. I have
 documented this experience thoroughly, including audio recordings of coerc=
ive meetings and video evidence of dismissal without cause or paperwork.</d=
iv>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
The evidence shows:</div>
<ul style=3D"text-align: left; margin: 0px 0px 1.5rem; padding-left: 1.5rem=
; list-style-position: outside; list-style-type: disc;">
<li style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, C=
alibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); line-h=
eight: 1.625; margin-left: 1rem;">
Park Manager Ryan Warren telling me to &quot;chew glass and swallow it&quot=
; as leadership advice</li><li style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedF=
ont, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; =
color: rgb(0, 0, 0); line-height: 1.625; margin-top: calc(0.5rem * calc(1 -=
 var(--tw-space-y-reverse))); margin-bottom: calc(0.5rem * var(--tw-space-y=
-reverse)); margin-left: 1rem;">
Admission that I was never given the benefit of the doubt from day one</li>=
<li style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, C=
alibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); line-h=
eight: 1.625; margin-top: calc(0.5rem * calc(1 - var(--tw-space-y-reverse))=
); margin-bottom: calc(0.5rem * var(--tw-space-y-reverse)); margin-left: 1r=
em;">
Two months of psychological pressure designed to force my resignation</li><=
li style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Ca=
libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); line-he=
ight: 1.625; margin-top: calc(0.5rem * calc(1 - var(--tw-space-y-reverse)))=
; margin-bottom: calc(0.5rem * var(--tw-space-y-reverse)); margin-left: 1re=
m;">
Weaponization of my identity and normal human communication as &quot;proble=
matic behavior&quot;</li><li style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFon=
t, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; co=
lor: rgb(0, 0, 0); line-height: 1.625; margin-top: calc(0.5rem * calc(1 - v=
ar(--tw-space-y-reverse))); margin-bottom: calc(0.5rem * var(--tw-space-y-r=
everse)); margin-left: 1rem;">
Dismissal six days before my scheduled completion, using fabricated pretens=
es</li></ul>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
This is not about whether misconduct occurred =97 it is documented. The onl=
y question is whether you will respond to documented misconduct with silenc=
e or with leadership.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 2rem; margin=
: 3rem 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
<b>My Concerns About Moving Forward</b></div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
I want to be direct about something that weighs on me: you have significant=
 institutional power, and I am aware that speaking publicly about documente=
d coercion and retaliation could result in further reprisal. Your connectio=
ns extend across state government
 and the parks community. You have resources I do not have. This power imba=
lance is real, and it factors into every decision I make about how to seek =
accountability.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
I am sharing this concern not to accuse you of anything, but to name the re=
ality that many volunteers face when considering whether to report miscondu=
ct. The very people who harm volunteers often have the institutional power =
to compound that harm through retaliation.
 It has literally already happened at Honeyman. This dynamic keeps abuse hi=
dden and allows harmful patterns to persist.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 2rem; margin=
: 3rem 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
<b>Why This Matters Beyond My Experience</b></div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
What happened to me at Honeyman was not unique=97it was systematic. The ins=
titutional response to documented misconduct has been complete silence, whi=
ch sends a clear message to other volunteers about what they can expect if =
they report harm. This creates an
 environment where unpaid service comes with exposure to psychological pres=
sure, and accountability requests disappear into administrative silence.</d=
iv>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
Volunteers are not disposable labor. We are community members who choose to=
 serve without compensation, often sacrificing time, income, and stability =
to support public institutions. We deserve basic protection from institutio=
nal retaliation, and we deserve
 leadership that responds to evidence of harm with presence rather than sil=
ence.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
Oregon Parks &amp; Recreation Department is facing budget challenges and ac=
tively recruiting community support through volunteer programs. But how can=
 you ask for community trust and unpaid labor while protecting managers who=
 systematically undermine and retaliate
 against those who answer that call?</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 2rem; margin=
: 3rem 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
<b>What Leadership Could Look Like</b></div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
I am not asking for apologies or personal remedies. I am asking for institu=
tional accountability that protects future volunteers from experiencing wha=
t I experienced. This could include:</div>
<ul style=3D"text-align: left; margin: 0px 0px 1.5rem; padding-left: 1.5rem=
; list-style-position: outside; list-style-type: disc;">
<li style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, C=
alibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); line-h=
eight: 1.625; margin-left: 1rem;">
Transparent investigation of the documented misconduct at Honeyman State Pa=
rk</li><li style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontSer=
vice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);=
 line-height: 1.625; margin-top: calc(0.5rem * calc(1 - var(--tw-space-y-re=
verse))); margin-bottom: calc(0.5rem * var(--tw-space-y-reverse)); margin-l=
eft: 1rem;">
Clear consequences for managers who deploy coercive tactics against volunte=
ers</li><li style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontSe=
rvice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)=
; line-height: 1.625; margin-top: calc(0.5rem * calc(1 - var(--tw-space-y-r=
everse))); margin-bottom: calc(0.5rem * var(--tw-space-y-reverse)); margin-=
left: 1rem;">
Systemic protections that prevent retaliation against volunteers who report=
 misconduct</li><li style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_=
MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(=
0, 0, 0); line-height: 1.625; margin-top: calc(0.5rem * calc(1 - var(--tw-s=
pace-y-reverse))); margin-bottom: calc(0.5rem * var(--tw-space-y-reverse));=
 margin-left: 1rem;">
Accessible grievance processes that don't depend on the good faith of the m=
anagers causing harm</li><li style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFon=
t, Aptos_MSFontService, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; co=
lor: rgb(0, 0, 0); line-height: 1.625; margin-top: calc(0.5rem * calc(1 - v=
ar(--tw-space-y-reverse))); margin-bottom: calc(0.5rem * var(--tw-space-y-r=
everse)); margin-left: 1rem;">
Training and oversight that ensures volunteer supervision meets basic profe=
ssional standards</li></ul>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
These are not extraordinary requests. They are basic institutional protecti=
ons that should exist in any organization that depends on unpaid community =
service.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 2rem; margin=
: 3rem 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
<b>The Choice Before You</b></div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
You have built a career on public service values and institutional leadersh=
ip. The question now is whether those values extend to protecting volunteer=
s when institutional loyalty conflicts with human accountability.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
The evidence of systematic misconduct at Honeyman State Park is public and =
permanent. Community awareness continues to grow. Every day of continued si=
lence becomes part of the documented institutional response to volunteer ha=
rm.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
This is not about whether you believe me. The recordings exist. The only ch=
oice is whether you meet that documentation with integrity or avoidance.</d=
iv>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 2rem; margin=
: 3rem 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
<b>My Commitment</b></div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
I want to be clear about my intentions. I am not appealing for personal rep=
air. There is no repair possible =97 the harm already happened, and it is r=
eal. I am documenting the record and naming the choice in front of you. The=
 documentation I have created exists
 to prevent future harm, not to punish past mistakes. If real accountabilit=
y emerges=97if systemic protections are implemented and harmful managers ar=
e held responsible=97this becomes a story of institutional learning rather =
than institutional failure.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
But accountability cannot happen through silence. It requires acknowledgmen=
t, investigation, and change. It requires leadership that chooses human dig=
nity over institutional self-protection.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
I remain hopeful that you will choose to be that leader.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
The volunteer community is watching. The Oregon community is watching. The =
question is not whether you have the power to address this=97you clearly do=
. The question is whether you will use that power to protect the people who=
 serve your institution, or to protect
 the institution from the people it has harmed.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
<b>In nearly fifty years of life, this was the worst institutional harm I h=
ave ever experienced. It deserved acknowledgment, not strategic avoidance.<=
/b></div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
Would you accept silence if this happened to someone you care about?</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
I was harmed, and others remain unprotected.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
Silence now only ensures it will happen again.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
Please choose wisely.</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
ice, Calibri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"=
 class=3D"elementToProof">
Respectfully,</div>
<div style=3D"text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; line-height: 1.625; margi=
n: 0px 0px 1.5rem; font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontServ=
